        "topic": "Depreciation Methods",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p>An asset costing $20,000 has a residual value of $2,000 and a useful life of 5 years. What is the annual depreciation using the straight-line method?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The straight-line depreciation formula is: <br><b>Annual Depreciation = (Cost - Residual Value) / Useful Life</b>. <br>Thus, ($20,000 - $2,000) / 5 = $3,600 per year.</p>",
